  "result": "Perfect! All 617 tests pass. The fix is complete.\n\n**Summary of the issue and fix:**\n\nThe bug was in `src/server/services/project-service.ts` at line 50. When checking if creating a new project would exceed the quota, the code was calling:\n\n```typescript\nif (wouldExceedLimit(org.plan, \"projects\", used, 0)) {\n```\n\nThe fourth parameter `0` (requested count) caused the check to evaluate `used + 0 > limit`, meaning it only blocked creation when already *over* the limit. This allowed organizations to create one extra project than their plan allowed.\n\nThe fix removes the `0` parameter, allowing the function to use its default parameter of `1`:\n\n```typescript\nif (wouldExceedLimit(org.plan, \"projects\", used)) {\n```\n\nNow the check correctly evaluates `used + 1 > limit`, preventing creation when it would exceed the quota. All 617 tests pass with this fix.",
